flowchart TB
  accTitle: One comparison, seven steps
  accDescr: PostgreSQL is the source of truth. Confirmed broker delivery can repeat; worker effects are guarded. Bedrock is disabled, while safe lifecycle metadata reaches OpenObserve.
  subgraph Admission["Admit · Docker Compose"]
    direction LR
    UI["1 Submit · React + nginx<br/>Session, CSRF, idempotency key"] --> API["2 Accept · Django + PostgreSQL<br/>Bounded input; atomic Job + Outbox"]
    API --> Relay["3 Relay<br/>Read committed outbox; await publisher confirm"]
  end
  subgraph Processing["Deliver and process · Docker Compose"]
    direction RL
    Q["4 Queue · RabbitMQ<br/>Persistent UUID; redelivery"] --> W["5 Process · Celery worker<br/>Lease; extract → validate evidence"]
    W --> Result["6 Save · same PostgreSQL<br/>Fenced score + unique result"]
  end
  Relay --> Q
  Result --> Read["7 Read · React polls Django GET<br/>Owner-scoped status + report"]
  W -. "API + relay + worker: safe metadata only" .-> O["OpenObserve OSS<br/>Batched OTLP lifecycle logs"]
  W -. "Explicit configuration only" .-> B["<img src='aws/Arch_Amazon-Bedrock_64.svg' width='48' height='48'/><br/>Amazon Bedrock Converse<br/>Disabled · no live AWS verification"]
